## Technical Comparison Overview

This system can be written in either **Python** (using the `requests` library) or as an optimized **Bash** wrapper (using `curl`). Below is how both patterns handle data formatting and submission:

| Operational Dimension | Python Pipeline (`run.py`) | Bash Alternative (`run.sh`) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Directory Traversal** | `os.listdir()` matrix array scanning | File descriptor glob loop (`for f in .../*`) |
| **Line Manipulation** | Slices by index (`lines[0]`, `lines[3:]`) | Precision text stream piping (`sed -n '1p'`) |
| **Data Formatting** | Native JSON key-value mapping objects | Escaped character payload serialization strings |
| **Transmission Protocol** | `requests.post(url, json=...)` | Multi-header curl query (`curl -X POST -H ...`) |
| **Target Success Code** | `201 Created` HTTP Response status | `201` HTTP Response validation output |

